    "perplexity": {
      "description": "...Best II is a 1992 compilation assembled after WEA acquired The Smiths’ back catalogue, collecting fourteen essential tracks from the band’s albums, singles, and B-sides. It moves from the jangling urgency of “The Headmaster Ritual,” “Still Ill,” and “Ask” to the sharper pop of “Heaven Knows I’m Miserable Now” and “Bigmouth Strikes Again,” while “Oscillate Wildly” highlights Johnny Marr’s instrumental craft. Morrissey’s melancholic, literate songwriting and Marr’s chiming, rhythmically intricate guitar work give the collection its distinctive blend of alternative rock, pop, and post-punk.\n\nThe second half is especially strong, pairing the theatrical “That Joke Isn’t Funny Anymore” and “Shakespeare’s Sister” with “Girl Afraid,” “Reel Around the Fountain,” “Last Night I Dreamt That Somebody Loved Me,” and the defining finale “There Is a Light That Never Goes Out.” As a companion to Best... I, it offers a concise overview of The Smiths’ most enduring material rather than a chronological narrative. The 2026 WEA vinyl release brings this long-unavailable compilation back to the format, making it a significant reissue for collectors and an accessible introduction to one of Britain’s most influential 1980s bands.",
